# Homepage

The publishing homepage introduces the service and prioritises important routes rather than linking to everything. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/homepage/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

For Home Assistant Overview, prioritise useful household status and frequent tasks. Keep current conditions separate from navigation. Room and domain names should be familiar, with visible labels beside meaningful native icons. The documentation homepage instead introduces the design system and its major learning routes.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a concise heading, a small number of task links and grouped secondary routes. Follow the local action-links component for navigational arrows. Whitespace and headings should do most of the grouping; do not surround every destination with a dark card border.

## Home Assistant boundary

A household homepage is not a clone of www.gov.uk. Use only civica.uk branding and supplied assets, never the crown or official masthead. Priorities depend on the household; do not infer universal “most used” tasks or fabricate live readings.

